<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Derivations</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We finish the derivation of expected objectives and violations of constraints in this section.
After defining communication overhead, we will compute its expectation and expected resource usage under regular scheduling before deriving the metrics essential to modulo scheduling</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Communication overhead</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In communication-bottlenecked workloads <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, we minimize the total edge length across all dependencies:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{Com}=\sum_{(v_{i},v_{j})\in E}s_{j}-s_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{Com}=\sum_{(v_{i},v_{j})\in E}s_{j}-s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then the expected total edge length <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{Com}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{Com}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of all expected violations from all edges:</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\widehat{L}}_{Com}=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{Com}]=\sum_{(v_{i},v_{j})\in E}\sum_{d_{i}=0}^{D-1}\sum_{d_{j}=d_{i}}^{D-1}P_{i}^{d_{i}}P_{j}^{d_{j}}\cdot(d_{j}-d_{i})\\
" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\widehat{L}}_{Com}=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{Com}]=\sum_{(v_{i},v_{j})\in E}\sum_{d_{i}=0}^{D-1}\sum_{d_{j}=d_{i}}^{D-1}P_{i}^{d_{i}}P_{j}^{d_{j}}\cdot(d_{j}-d_{i})\\
</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Expected Resource Usage</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To represent the expected resource usage at step <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, we reuse the probability that an operator <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with resource demand <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is active at that step defined in Equation <a href="#S3.EGx4" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
The expected resource usage is the sum of individual usage:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Res}(d)=\mathbb{E}[Res(d)]=\sum_{v_{i}\in V}w_{i}\cdot P_{i}^{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Res}(d)=\mathbb{E}[Res(d)]=\sum_{v_{i}\in V}w_{i}\cdot P_{i}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To optimize for peak resource utilization, we apply the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LogSumExp</span> operator across all steps <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\{0,\dots,D-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\{0,\dots,D-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is similar to the computation of global memory footprint in <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{Res}\approx\tau\cdot\log\left(\sum_{d}\exp\left(\frac{{\widehat{Res}(d)}}{\tau}\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>d</mi></munder><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{Res}\approx\tau\cdot\log\left(\sum_{d}\exp\left(\frac{{\widehat{Res}(d)}}{\tau}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define the violations as the number of exceeded resources used summed across all steps.
Then the expected violations can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{Res}=\sum_{d}\text{ReLU}\left(\widehat{{Res}}(d)-R\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>d</mi></munder><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{Res}=\sum_{d}\text{ReLU}\left(\widehat{{Res}}(d)-R\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a given resources limit, and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ReLU}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ReLU}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> ensures only exceeding resources are counted toward violations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Modulo Metrics</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a pipeline, an operator scheduled at step <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> consumes resources at steps <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\mod{II}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>mod</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\mod{II}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The probability that operator <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> occupies a resource at time <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\dots,II-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\dots,II-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> within the modulo reservation table is the sum of its probabilities across all linear steps that map to <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P\left\{\lfloor X_{i}+0.5\rfloor=t\right\}=\sum_{k=0}^{\lceil D/\text{II}\rceil}P_{i}^{t+k\cdot II}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\left\{\lfloor X_{i}+0.5\rfloor=t\right\}=\sum_{k=0}^{\lceil D/\text{II}\rceil}P_{i}^{t+k\cdot II}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{t+k\cdot\text{II}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{t+k\cdot\text{II}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the probability of scheduling operator <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to step <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=t+k\cdot\text{II}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=t+k\cdot\text{II}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in Equation <a href="#S3.E7.2" title="Equation 7b ‣ Equation 7 ‣ 3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7b</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modulo Resource Usage</span>.
Similar to the derivation in <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>,
at step <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t&lt;\text{II}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t&lt;\text{II}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected modulo resource usage <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{MRes}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{MRes}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{MRes}(t)=\sum_{v_{i}\in V}w_{i}\cdot P\left\{\lfloor X_{i}+0.5\rfloor=t\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{MRes}(t)=\sum_{v_{i}\in V}w_{i}\cdot P\left\{\lfloor X_{i}+0.5\rfloor=t\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modulo Memory Footprint</span>.
Memory footprint in a pipeline is similarly wrapped.
A memory unit carrying the output of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is active at step <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> if it is active at any time step <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=t+k\cdot\text{II},k&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=t+k\cdot\text{II},k&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the linear probability <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(X_{i}\leq s&lt;\max_{v_{j}\in succ(v_{i})}X_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(X_{i}\leq s&lt;\max_{v_{j}\in succ(v_{i})}X_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Equation <a href="#S3.E9.2" title="Equation 9b ‣ Equation 9 ‣ 3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9b</span></a>, we can compute the modulo expectation:</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{MReg}(t)=\sum_{v_{i}\in V}b_{i}\cdot\sum_{k=0}^{\lceil D/\text{II}\rceil}P\left\{d_{i}\leq t+k\cdot\text{II}&lt;\max_{v_{j}\in{succ(i)}}d_{j}\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></munderover><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>II</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{MReg}(t)=\sum_{v_{i}\in V}b_{i}\cdot\sum_{k=0}^{\lceil D/\text{II}\rceil}P\left\{d_{i}\leq t+k\cdot\text{II}&lt;\max_{v_{j}\in{succ(i)}}d_{j}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The expected maximum modulo resource usage and peak memory footprint can be computed using <span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LogSumExp</span> similar to Equation <a href="#S3.E10.2" title="Equation 10b ‣ Equation 10 ‣ 3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10b</span></a>.
The expected violations can be computed using ReLU similar to Equation <a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ B.2 Expected Resource Usage ‣ Appendix B Derivations ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recurrence Violations</span>.
For modulo scheduling with loop-carried dependencies, a back-edge from producer <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to consumer <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with an iteration distance <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and latency Lat<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> imposes the constraint <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}+k\cdot\text{II}\geq s_{j}+\text{Lat}(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Lat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}+k\cdot\text{II}\geq s_{j}+\text{Lat}(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let the set of these dependencies be defined as <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{j},v_{i},k)\in E_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{j},v_{i},k)\in E_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similar to the computation of expected dependency violations in Equation <a href="#S3.EGx5" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.2 Representing Objectives and Constraints ‣ 3 Method ‣ GauS: Differentiable Scheduling Optimization via Gaussian Reparameterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>,
the expected recurrence violation <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{rec}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{rec}</annotation></semantics></math> is formulated by summing the probabilities of all invalid steps assignments <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d_{i},d_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d_{i},d_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> that fail to satisfy the recurrence constraint:</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\widehat{V}}_{Rec}=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{V}_{Rec}]=\sum_{(v_{i},v_{j},k)\in E_{B}}\sum_{d_{i}=1}^{D-1}\sum_{d_{j}=d_{i}+k\cdot\text{II}+1}^{D-1}P_{i}^{d_{i}}\cdot P_{j}^{d_{j}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>II</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\widehat{V}}_{Rec}=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{V}_{Rec}]=\sum_{(v_{i},v_{j},k)\in E_{B}}\sum_{d_{i}=1}^{D-1}\sum_{d_{j}=d_{i}+k\cdot\text{II}+1}^{D-1}P_{i}^{d_{i}}\cdot P_{j}^{d_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Detailed Evaluation Setup</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Experiment Setup</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Environment Settings</span>.
All the experiments are performed on a Linux server equipped two NVIDIA A100 GPUs with 80 GB memory and two AMD EPYC 9124 CPUs (2<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>16 cores) running at 3.7 GHz, 1.5 TB of RAM.
For softwares, we use PyTorch 2.5.1 with CUDA 12.1, Gurobi 13.0, and CPLEX 22.1.1.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyper-parameter Settings</span>.
We use a uniform set of hyperparameters across all problem instances and formulations.
We use the Adam optimizer with a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The penalty parameter <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, used to enforce constraints, is set to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>;
the <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LogSumExp</span> temperature parameter <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>;
the initialization freedom parameter <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Dataset Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the random workload (RW) evaluations, we utilize a subset of the datasets released by GS-Schedule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>,
though our selected subset is substantially larger than the one featured in the original study to better evaluate scalability.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T1" class="ltx_table">
